# Mechanism Kind end-to-end validation case
#
# Targets T2.1 (mechanism Kind in ERM) + T2.2 (mechanism scan pipeline).
# The question asks "how does ContinuationPrompt work?" which should:
#   1. extract a `mechanism` ERM Kind from "怎么实现"
#   2. resolve `ContinuationPrompt` as the target function
#   3. extractDecisionBlocks find its top-level branches
#   4. mechanism_scan emit EvidenceMechanism items per branch
#   5. answerPredicateWhitelist (T1.3) accept mechanism predicates so
#      they reach Ground Truth
#   6. final answer enumerates the actual strategies, not a generic
#      "it returns a prompt" hand-wave
#
# Expected substrings come from the canonical strategy list in
# reference_explorer_eval_methodology (T3 ground truth):
#   - function-boundary read guidance
#   - enumeration completeness push
#   - idle streak / idle termination
ID="df3"
NAME="ContinuationPrompt mechanism enumeration"
QUESTION="explorerEvaluator 的 ContinuationPrompt 是怎么实现的?有哪几种 push 策略?"
#
# Verdict strategy: positive substrings verify the answer is anchored
# on the right entity; negative substrings forbid the specific failure
# mode (drifting into sibling evaluators' same-named methods).
#
# Previous attempt used `partial` / `enumeration` as positive substrings
# to verify strategy enumeration, but those failed on correct Chinese
# answers where the LLM paraphrased into `函数边界` / `枚举完整性`
# instead of keeping the English terms. Structural anchors that survive
# bilingual paraphrase are the only reliable positive signal.
#
# Positive substrings (AND, all required):
#   - ContinuationPrompt       entity name — always kept as code identifier
#   - explorer.go              grounded in the right source file
#   - explorerEvaluator        the receiver type, disambiguates from
#                              subExplorerEvaluator / finalizerEvaluator
#
# Negative substrings (none may appear): the three sibling evaluators
# that all have a ContinuationPrompt method but are NOT the target.
# A correct answer that is scoped to explorerEvaluator will never need
# to mention these sibling names. Their presence is dispositive evidence
# of the "polymorphic method drift" failure mode (see the 15-run audit
# on df3-{151444,173231,181104} where every "PASS" green-washed an
# answer citing subExplorerEvaluator.ContinuationPrompt's trivial
# `return "", false`).
EXPECT_CONTAINS="ContinuationPrompt explorer.go explorerEvaluator"
EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS="subExplorerEvaluator finalizerEvaluator"
